<title>CHILE: Chile Oct copper exports slump on lower prices.</title>
<headline>Chile Oct copper exports slump on lower prices.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean copper exports fell sharply in terms of value to $496.9 million from $581.1 million in the same month last year as the result of tumbling world copper prices, said the central bank.</p>
<p>A steady rise in the volume of exports failed to make up for a 30 percent slide in prices over the last 12 months, said the report.</p>
<p>The following are details of Chile's mining exports in October:  </p>
<p> METAL			   Oct 1996	    Oct 1995</p>
<p> Copper			  496.9		 581.1</p>
<p> Iron				6.9		   8.7</p>
<p> Salitre and iodine	   17.6		  10.0</p>
<p> Silver			   13.3		  13.4</p>
<p> Molybdenum		     15.4		  35.8</p>
<p> Lithium carbonate	     3.6		   3.8</p>
<p> Metallic gold and dor     36.7		  41.1</p>
<p> Gold mineral		    5.4		   9.0</p>
<p> Others			   12.1		   6.4</p>
<p> TOTAL			   607.9		 707.5</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures are in millions of dollars.</p>
<p>-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212</p>
</text>
